# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-***

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials for coding engineers (off by default; see "Coding agents" in README.md)
# Each engineer has a sign-in of its own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recommended: subscriptions
# claude-1: the OAuth token printed by `claude setup-token`
# CLAUDE_1_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# codex-1: a ChatGPT sign-in made for codex-1 only. Create it with
#   mkdir -p ~/.codex-1 && CODEX_HOME=~/.codex-1 codex login
# then paste the output of `jq -c . ~/.codex-1/auth.json` inside single quotes.
# CODEX_1_AUTH_JSON='{"auth_mode":"chatgpt", ...}'

# Other options
# codex-1 on ChatGPT Enterprise: an access token from the workspace's Access tokens page.
# Set this or CODEX_1_AUTH_JSON, not both.
# CODEX_1_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# API keys: claude-1 uses ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, codex-1 uses OPENAI_API_KEY above.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JWT verification for AgentOS. Generate your JWT_VERIFICATION_KEY at os.agno.com.
# In production, the app refuses to serve traffic without a JWT_VERIFICATION_KEY or JWT_JWKS_FILE.
# For initial Render setup, use RUNTIME_ENV=dev in the dashboard.
# Then set RUNTIME_ENV=prd with the verification key and redeploy; see README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quote the value so parsers read the multi-line PEM as one variable:
# JWT_VERIFICATION_KEY="-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
# MIIBIjANBgkq...
# -----END PUBLIC KEY-----"
# JWT_JWKS_FILE=/app/jwks.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AgentOS URL used by the scheduler and MCP server.
# Set this to the public URL of your AgentOS instance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENTOS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MCP OAuth — set MCP_CONNECT_SECRET to turn the /mcp endpoint into its own
# OAuth 2.1 authorization server, which is how claude.ai and ChatGPT (web) connect.
# Connecting to the MCP server asks for this secret on a consent page.
# Generate a strong one (≥16 chars):
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MCP_CONNECT_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web access uses Parallel SDK when authenticated,
# and falls back to Parallel's keyless MCP server for local development.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PARALLEL_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Slack — set both to enable the Slack interface.
#   SLACK_BOT_TOKEN       Bot User OAuth Token (xoxb-***)
#   SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET  Signing Secret (Basic Information → App Credentials)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DB_HOST=localhost
# DB_PORT=5432
# DB_USER=ai
# DB_PASS=ai
# DB_DATABASE=ai
# DB_DRIVER=postgresql+psycopg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional GitHub access for coding agents (forwarded to sandboxes).
# Every engineer run uses this one token, so a push carries the token's rights, not the
# rights of the person who asked. Use a fine-grained token limited to this one repository
# that can push branches and open pull requests (Contents and Pull requests: Read and
# write), with no admin rights. Protect main so nothing lands without a review.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GH_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_READ_TOKEN=             # Optional separate private-checkout token; defaults to GH_TOKEN.
# With either token set, Super Agent can also read GitHub itself: pull requests, diffs, checks
# and files. It is given functions that read only, and uses GITHUB_READ_TOKEN when it is set.
# Commits default to AgentOS <agentos@localhost>. Override the author/committer:
# GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=
# GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=
# GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=
# GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=

# Local setup: scripts/aws.py reads these settings from .env.
# AWS_PROFILE=your-profile
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# DEPLOYMENT_NAME=agentos-sandbox
# BUCKET_NAME=your-checkpoint-bucket  # Omit to derive a name.
# CHECKPOINT_PREFIX=agentos/checkpoints/

# After setup: add the printed values to your API host's environment.
# AGENTCORE_RUNTIME_ARN=
# AGENTCORE_CHECKPOINT_BUCKET=
# AGENTCORE_CHECKPOINT_PREFIX=agentos/checkpoints/
